g of water in urban or other\nareas is occurring or is imminent.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 226 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. This may cause urban and small stream flooding. Up\nto 0.5 inches of rain have fallen.\n\n- Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1 inch are expected over\nthe area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nDenver, Aurora, eastern Centennial, Englewood, Greenwood Village,\nSheridan, Buckley SFB, Arapahoe Park, Cherry Hills Village,\nFoxfield and Cherry Creek Reservoir.","ends":"2026-08-15T16:30:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Adams, CO; Arapahoe, CO; Denver, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d1f99c4123bab47c11a356083c849ccd983e7854.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d1f99c4123bab47c11a356083c849ccd983e7854.001.1"},{"event":"Special Weather Statement","headline":"Special Weather Statement issued August 15 at 2:08PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"At 208 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a line of strong\nthunderstorms extending from over Lakewood to over Castle Rock, or\nextending from 11 miles west of Denver to 23 miles south of Denver,\nmoving northeast at 10 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and half inch size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor damage to outdoor objects is\npossible.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nDenver, southwestern Aurora, Lakewood, southeastern Arvada,\nCentennial, Highlands Ranch, Castle Rock, Parker, Littleton,\nEnglewood, Wheat Ridge, Greenwood Village, Lone Tree, Sheridan,\nMorrison, Castle Pines, The Pinery and Franktown.","ends":"2026-08-15T14:45:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Boulder And Jefferson Counties Below 6000 Feet/West Broomfield County; North Douglas County Below 6000 Feet/Denver/West Adams and Arapahoe Counties/East Broomfield 